.el .ds Aq '
.TH grex-add 1  "grex-add "
.SH NAME
grex\-add \- Register a pack — appends an `Event::Add` to `.grex/events.jsonl` and inserts a `{url, path, ref?}` row into `.grex/pack.yaml`\*(Aqs `children:` sequence. `pack.yaml` is created from the minimal v1 skeleton when absent so `sync`/`ls`/`status` see the pack immediately (v1.4.1: closes the bridge that v1.4.0 left unwired)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgrex\-add\fR [\fB\-\-ref\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a pack — appends an `Event::Add` to `.grex/events.jsonl` and inserts a `{url, path, ref?}` row into `.grex/pack.yaml`\*(Aqs `children:` sequence. `pack.yaml` is created from the minimal v1 skeleton when absent so `sync`/`ls`/`status` see the pack immediately (v1.4.1: closes the bridge that v1.4.0 left unwired)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fI<GIT\-REF>\fR
v1.3.3 B10 — git ref to pin at add time. Accepts `<branch>`, `<commit>` (7..40 hex chars), or `<branch>@<commit>` (single flag, `@` delimiter). When omitted, defaults to the remote\*(Aqs `main` branch HEAD per the 8\-cell folder\-FA design
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
Git URL of the pack repo
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Optional local path (defaults to repo name)
